eue exists to let priority reorder processing, since the server handles one TCP connection at a time. An out-of-enum value is rejected format-only (`E311`). Absence of `priority` leaves the response unchanged (additive, no regression). Verified live end-to-end on a real TCP connection (`examples/priority_escalation_smoke_test.rs`, 6 scenarios: no `priority` unchanged, `critical` escalates, `high`/`normal`/`low` annotate without escalating, an invalid value rejected with `E311`). |
